wasm has no floating-point exception support, so wasix-libc's <fenv.h> defines
no exception-flag macros (FE_INVALID etc.); only FE_ALL_EXCEPT/FE_TONEAREST
(both 0) and no-op fe* stubs exist. H5T__init_native_float_types() masks FP
exceptions with feholdexcept()/feclearexcept(FE_INVALID)/feupdateenv() while
probing "don't care" bits of NaNs; FE_INVALID is undeclared and the masking is
pointless on wasm. Guard the whole fe* dance (and its saved_fenv, else unused)
for __wasi__.

Recheck if wasix-libc grows FP exception support (FE_INVALID and real fe*).
